{
"host": "#fhTellBands",
"caption": "Per-band summary of the telluric line list (<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gordon2026\">Gordon et al. 2026</a>, HITRAN2024; 40 line groups) and the broad continua (collision-induced absorption from the HITRAN CIA 2024 files, <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-karman2019\">Karman et al. 2019</a>, with the original laboratory references; O₃ from <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-serdyuchenko2014\">Serdyuchenko et al. 2014</a> at 223 K). Model: AFGL-1986 U.S. Standard atmosphere (<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-anderson1986\">Anderson et al. 1986</a>) seen from sea level at airmass 1, PWV 14.2 mm, 344 DU O₃, CO₂/CH₄/N₂O scaled to NOAA 2025 means. Air wavelengths are derived with <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-peck1972\">Peck &amp; Reeder 1972</a> (fitted to 1.69 µm, extrapolated beyond). Depths are for isolated lines; ΣEW double-counts overlapping lines and so exceeds the true band absorption in saturated H₂O bands. Continuum peaks are maxima of smoothed tables on ≈ 1 cm⁻¹ or 0.01 nm grids: these features are tens to hundreds of Å wide and have no mÅ position. Numbers with trailing zeros are shown as numbers (e.g. 7632.158 = 7632.1580).",
